aximize my probability of winning. I'm going to go for it.\n\n\n", 'output': "Evaluation: The current hand is Two Pair (2s and 3s) on a board of K-J-2-3. The opponent has shown passivity throughout the hand (checking pre-flop and flop) and then suddenly escalated to an All-in check-raise on the turn over a small bet. This massive overbet (likely ~50x the pot) is inconsistent with a nut hand like a Set or Top Two Pair, which would typically seek value rather than forcing a fold. The line is more indicative of a vulnerable Top Pair (e.g., Kx) trying to protect against draws, or a pure bluff/semi-bluff (flush draw). Since Two Pair beats all one-pair hands and bluffs, and given that you are currently losing the match and need a significant chip swing to take the lead, calling is the strategically correct move to capitalize on the opponent's likely error or weaker range.\n\nReason: You hold Two Pair, which is a strong hand. The opponent's massive overbet shove on the Turn after checking previous streets suggests they are likely holding a vulnerable top pair or bluffing, rather than holding a monster hand like a set (which would value bet). Calling gives you the best chance to double up and take the lead in the game.\n\nAnswer: -2"}
