lling risks ~20,000 chips, which, if lost, would slash my lead and potentially allow the opponent to overtake me in the final hand. Folding costs a negligible amount (the blinds) and effectively guarantees that I win the match, as the opponent cannot overcome the chip deficit in the single remaining hand without me voluntarily losing a massive pot. There is no incentive to take this risk.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
